WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:05.900
It's crazy that we haven't had a live-action
Star Wars show yet, but in 2019, it's finally

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:06.400
happening.

00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:09.580
It's been a long time coming, but we have
a little bit of information about the very

00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:14.420
first live-action Star Wars series, The Mandalorian,
and we can't wait to share it with you.

00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:17.080
A frontier far, far away

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:21.060
They say the Star Wars universe has room for
an infinite number of stories, and now we

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:23.620
know what this particular story is, kind of.

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:29.100
In October 2018, series creator and writer
Jon Favreau made a post on Instagram laying

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:29.940
out the basics.

00:00:30.109 --> 00:00:34.640
According to Favreau, the new Star Wars show
will focus on "the travails of a lone gunfighter

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:38.380
in the outer reaches of the galaxy far from
the authority of the New Republic."

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:43.150
The "lone gunfighter" phrase is telling, making
it sound like The Mandalorian will be a space-flavored

00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:47.620
take on the western genre, treating outer
space like the lawless expanse that it is.

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:52.160
"Point is, it's just us, out here."

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:54.420
Star Wars already owes a debt to westerns.

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:58.760
The story goes that George Lucas screened
Sergio Leone's Once Upon a Time in the West

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:02.360
for the Star Wars crew before filming, and
that's an easy story to believe.

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:06.740
The original Star Wars trilogy is full of
nods to classic westerns, heck, Star Wars'

00:01:06.759 --> 00:01:11.010
sound editors reportedly even gave Boba Fett
the sound of spurs jangling when he walks.

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:13.720
It looks like The Mandalorian will lean into
the genre, too.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:15.220
Manda-what?

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:19.869
In Star Wars lore, Mandalorians are fierce
warriors with a long, proud, and surprisingly

00:01:19.869 --> 00:01:20.869
complex history.

00:01:20.869 --> 00:01:25.100
You may not have seen them before, but you're
probably familiar with their most iconic outfits.

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:30.100
Boba Fett wears Mandalorian armor, as did
his father, the bounty hunter Jango Fett.

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:33.240
Despite their fashion sense, they aren't Mandalorians
themselves.

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:37.840
Mandalore has never played a role in the movies,
and you won't ever actually hear the word

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:39.100
"Mandalorian" in the original trilogy.

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:43.480
But the society and its struggles are a big
part of Star Wars' different animated series.

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:48.240
In The Clone Wars, Mandalore is a place ravaged
by centuries of war, with the chaos being

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:52.680
severe enough to provide an opening for none
other than Darth Maul to conquer the planet.

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:56.280
Naturally, he uses it as a headquarters for
his criminal syndicate.

00:01:56.380 --> 00:02:00.880
Sabine Wren, one of the main characters on
Star Wars Rebels, is also a Mandalorian, one

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:04.320
who plays an important part in quelling the
society's warring ways.

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:05.500
Edge of the world

00:02:05.860 --> 00:02:09.670
During an interview at the premiere of Solo,
Jon Favreau went ahead and explained when

00:02:09.670 --> 00:02:13.840
The Mandalorian is supposed to take place,
and the time period sounds full of opportunity.

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:18.280
Favreau explained that The Mandalorian takes
place about seven years after Return of the

00:02:18.290 --> 00:02:21.250
Jedi, or roughly two decades before The Force
Awakens.

00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:25.950
By this point, the Rebel Alliance has transformed
into the New Republic, while the former Imperials

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:29.610
who'd eventually form the First Order are
still licking their wounds in the galaxy's

00:02:29.610 --> 00:02:30.620
Unknown Regions.

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:34.840
The Mandalorian is purported to have a remote
setting, taking place far away from the New

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:39.000
Republic, so we'd be surprised to see any
characters from the movies show up.

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:43.250
When The Mandalorian takes place, Luke would
be busy scouring the galaxy for Force-sensitive

00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:45.200
artifacts and old Jedi knowledge.

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:49.100
Poe would still be a little kid, Finn would
be an infant, and Rey wouldn't even have been

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:49.860
born yet.

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:51.860
One big Rebels connection

00:02:52.340 --> 00:02:55.520
Jon Favreau isn't adapting Star Wars to the
small screen on his own.

00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:57.180
"There is another."

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:02.400
The Iron Man director is also getting a hand
from a creator some fans will recognize: Dave

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:02.900
Filoni.

00:03:03.020 --> 00:03:06.780
He may not be a household name, but if you're
a modern day Star Wars fan, you probably know

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:07.280
his work.

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:11.480
Filoni directed The Clone Wars feature film,
which, let's face it, isn't really something

00:03:11.480 --> 00:03:12.240
to brag about.

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:16.840
But he also worked side-by-side with George
Lucas to bring the subsequent, superior animated

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:17.980
series to the air.

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:22.340
Filoni also co-created both Rebels and the
newest Star Wars cartoon, Resistance.

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:26.380
In other words, he's the guy behind a lot
of the best of parts modern Star Wars canon.

00:03:26.380 --> 00:03:31.130
According to The Art of Star Wars: The Clone
Wars, Filoni is the brains behind Anakin Skywalker's

00:03:31.130 --> 00:03:33.200
beloved apprentice, Ahsoka Tano.

00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:37.300
On Rebels, Filoni and his staff raised questions
about the Jedi's relationship with the Force

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:38.590
years before The Last Jedi.

00:03:38.590 --> 00:03:41.750
He even voiced Chopper, Rebels' scene-stealing
droid.

00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:45.340
Now, Filoni will be bringing his take on Star
Wars to The Mandalorian, too.

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:49.680
He's one of the show's executive producers,
and he'll make his live-action directing debut

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:52.000
by helming The Mandalorian's very first episode.

00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:53.960
The other big Rebels connection

00:03:54.260 --> 00:03:56.000
We're about to get into spoiler territory.

00:03:56.180 --> 00:04:00.040
If you haven't seen the series finale of Star
Wars Rebels yet, you may want to duck out

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:00.840
for this part.

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:05.370
While The Mandalorian has a title, a premise,
and a setting in time, it still doesn't have

00:04:05.370 --> 00:04:07.300
a cast, at least, not one that's been announced.

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:08.819
But we do have some ideas.

00:04:08.819 --> 00:04:12.950
Shortly after the series was announced, a
theory emerged that the mysterious lead character

00:04:12.950 --> 00:04:17.239
of The Mandalorian is none other than the
demolitions expert and Star Wars Rebels star

00:04:17.240 --> 00:04:18.140
Sabine Wren.

00:04:18.310 --> 00:04:21.800
The series ends with Sabine and Ahsoka on
a quest to find the villains Thrawn and Ezra

00:04:21.810 --> 00:04:25.760
after the fall of the Empire, the sort of
mission that could conceivably take somebody

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:27.360
to the very edge of known space.

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:31.000
Sabine's got the right ancestry, too, and
it does seem curious that we haven't seen

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:32.080
our hero's face yet.

00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:35.540
Throw in Filoni's involvement and the fact
that, hey, that really could be a woman in

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:40.000
there, and you've got a decent argument that
Sabine is the Mandalorian of the series title.

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:44.290
Maybe it's a long shot, but what's in store
will be exciting to watch unfold either way.

00:04:44.290 --> 00:04:47.500
We'll find out more when the series touches
down in 2019.

